※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4663

※ A division answers with a result, and by zero it answers one that holds
※ nothing.  Where the number has to be known while compiling there is nothing
※ to take out of it, so `?` over it is refused; `??` says what to have instead.

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    let t: 〈u8, u16〉 = 〈1u8, 2u16〉
    let a: u8 = t⟦(1 ÷ 0)?⟧
    0u6
